config ZMK_INPUT_PROCESSOR_MOUSE_LAYER_GATE
    bool "Movement-gated temporary mouse layer input processor"
    default y if DT_HAS_ZMK_INPUT_PROCESSOR_MOUSE_LAYER_GATE_ENABLED
    depends on ZMK_POINTING
    depends on !ZMK_SPLIT || ZMK_SPLIT_ROLE_CENTRAL
    help
      Input processor that only activates a temporary layer after the
      trackball has moved a configurable distance inside a short time
      window, then deactivates it again after an idle timeout.

      Unlike zmk,input-processor-temp-layer, tiny bumps and chassis
      vibrations do not switch layers, and pressing a non-transparent
      key on the target layer restarts the idle timeout.
